[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station draining the southern slopes of Ben Nevis. GENERAL: Velocity area station; about 20m wide river section with boulder control. STATION HYDROMETRY: All flows contained. Difficulty in gauging low flows results in a scattered low flow rating. Ratings derived from current meter gaugings up to 118 cumecs (about 0.95 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7). FLOW REGIME: Very responsive regime. Flows are largely natural although runoff from 6.7 sq.km of the headwaters diverted to Loch Trieg for hydro-electric power and further downstream around 5% of Q95 is abstracted for public water supply.
CATCHMENT,Wet, steep-sided, high altitude catchment draining southern slopes of Ben Nevis. No storage. Largely impermeable bedrock with approx. 1/3 overlain by superficial deposits. Predominantly Moinian metamorphic with limestone and granitic intrusions. Prolonged winter snow cover. Moorland, rough pasture, and some forestry. No significant catchment changes known.
Qmed Suitability,No comment.
Pooling Suitability,No comment.
